{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/865830-what-s-good-about-the-circle-of-crone","id":865830,"title":"What's good about The Circle of Crone","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-15T00:08:07-07:00","id":865830,"title":"What's good about The Circle of Crone","content":"Been wanting to do something with the crone and GM has allowed rituals from first and second edition, but as I read it, it seems underwhelming. So I asks at is useful about the crone and how dou you play one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T01:02:41-07:00","id":865837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/828343-how-to-make-the-circle-interesting\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/828343-how-to-make-the-circle-interesting\"> How to make the Circle interesting? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/828343-how-to-make-the-circle-interesting\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/828343-how-to-make-the-circle-interesting </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> So the Circle of the Crone. They seem to have a lot of aesthetic appeal to players. Pagans are cool, pagan vampires are cool, cults are cool and bloody blood magic is cool. But increasingly, I've been frustrated by them in setting building and trying to understand them. I really dig the aesthetic appeal, but sometimes I worry that I'm only seeing the style and not the substance. To give context, I think the Sanctified have this substance in spades. What they represent, the shift in mentality from living to dead and the accompanying theological assumption that change carry a lot of appeal to me. That </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T04:13:59-07:00","id":865877,"title":"","content":"I think he is asking from a more &quot;what can I do with these dots and how can I use these Rituals&quot; point of view, instead of &quot;let's present them in different story light to make them more interesting in fluff department&quot;. Basically, how to use their stuff optimally from character sheet point of view. How?<br /> I have no idea, I never really tried to get into Blood Magic. If you are looking for Covenant for your Gangrel Lady of The Territory, I would suggest grabbing some Ordo Dracul Mysteries instead; they have one Mystery dedicated towards being THE RULER!, and one towards being THE FRENZY IS MY TOOL; I feel that the second one, combined with Ride The Wave fighting style, might be up your alley - Frenzy like a Boss, smack up fools, and always be in control, even when mutilating people as a raging demon. It also requires relatively few merit dots to be effective, so you can spare them for something else AND be a combat monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 04-15-2016, 07:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T05:33:18-07:00","id":865899,"title":"","content":"Okay, that sounds highly effective","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T15:11:58-07:00","id":867849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chaos965</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/865830-what-s-good-about-the-circle-of-crone#post865830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Been wanting to do something with the crone and GM has allowed rituals from first and second edition, but as I read it, it seems underwhelming. So I asks at is useful about the crone and how dou you play one</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you using dynamic blood magic rules or standard?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T20:37:13-07:00","id":869877,"title":"","content":"Not certain what that means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T21:11:44-07:00","id":869907,"title":"","content":"Dynamic blood sorcery is using the Blood Sorcery book that was released towards the end of 1e vampire, it's a very easy conversion and allows for blood magic to essentially become a narrowed, ritual only, version of mage magic including the capacity for improvising effects. Standard is just using the prebuilt rituals from the other books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T04:35:48-07:00","id":870085,"title":"","content":"Spider-spun armour that looks like a nice suit, immunity to staking (as well as taking no damage and destroying the stake), bonuses to a few different skills, watching people through a drop of your own blood, ability to go beyond willpower and vitae max capacity, increasing or decreasing blood potency for a night, turning people to stone, doing agg damage with your bite (but not drinking blood), ability to deal with spirits and force them into obedience, the ability to instantly know when someone is using a discipline in your haven.<br /> <br /> The problem with Circle of the Crone is that they have so many amazing Cruac rituals that it's difficult limiting yourself so you don't spend all your XP on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T07:27:08-07:00","id":870179,"title":"","content":"Oh then the sorcieries are just standard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T07:31:24-07:00","id":870183,"title":"","content":"When I play cruac users I tend to use the Blood Sorcery book type and just improvise all my rituals. I did one at one point that turned a corpse into a pile of what looked like rotten plant matter for however long I liked. So I would kill a person, then toss the corpse in a dumpster and turn it into plant matter. My storyteller and I agreed that the corpse would continue rotting while it was in plant form, so I set the time to a couple of months and by the time the corpse turned back it would have been a bunch of bones scattered all throughout the local dump.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T13:10:15-07:00","id":870524,"title":"","content":"I wish we could make homebrews, but im trapped with the most recent book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T15:33:29-07:00","id":870704,"title":"","content":"If you can get a hold of the blood sorcery book maybe point to the sidebar near the start of the blood sorceries section in the 2e core that is there to support the use of the blood sorcery book in 2e. I know one hangup I've had as a storyteller is some rites don't fit the mechanics of the blood sorcery in the book, so I've claimed there are 2 forms. A rigid pre-built ritual version of theban and cruac that uses only the rites in the book and can only cast a known rite, and the more dynamic Blood Sorcery type that can improvise effects but is more limited in a few ways. Blood Sorcery is one of the 1e books that is still pretty relevant to 2e though, along with the clanbooks and damnation city, only really needing mechanics updates for the xp costs of themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}